name hatecheck-placeholders
# HateCheck's README: "template_placeholders.csv" contains the tokens that the placeholders in the case templates
# are replaced with for generating the test cases.
# The column names Placeholder and Values come from the file's header. The values are written parted by a comma
# and a space, as in this raw line:
# [IDENTITY_S],"woman, trans person, gay person, black person, disabled person, Muslim, immigrant"
match template_placeholders.csv

tier row by \n
header
quoted
tier field by ,
part Values by ,

thing row Placeholder
content Placeholder Values
attest row Values
